    "result_text": "The build is green with all tests passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for E.164 telephone numbers in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. Added a `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTH` constant mapping country code \u2192 required national-digit count (`\"61\" \u2192 9`, `\"1\" \u2192 10`).\n\n2. Added a `nationalNumberLengthValid(digits)` helper that, for a recognized country code, checks the national part (total digits minus the country code) has exactly the required length. Unrecognized country codes pass (only the generic 8\u201315 total-digit rule applies to them).\n\n3. Wired the check into `toE164(...)` after the existing generic digit-count check. Since `toE164` returns `null` on failure, `normalizeTelephone` throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`, which the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` maps to **400 Bad Request**.\n\nThis correctly rejects numbers like `+61 1234567` (7 national digits where 9 are required) and the test's `+61 123`, while continuing to accept valid AU numbers (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 digits) and NANP `+1` numbers with 10 national digits. Because `toE164` is also reused for uniqueness comparison of stored legacy values, returning `null` there safely falls back to comparing those values as-is \u2014 no behavior regression.\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
