    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing structure:\n\n- `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTH` is placed with the other validation constants (`EMAIL_PATTERN`, the max-owners constant) and is documented in the same style.\n- The per-country check is extracted into a focused private helper, `nationalNumberLengthValid`, mirroring how the file already factors validation logic into small private methods rather than inlining everything.\n- The new guard is inserted into `toE164`, which the Javadoc already designates as \"the single authoritative definition of a telephone's normalized form\" \u2014 so the new rule lives in exactly the right unit and automatically applies everywhere normalization is used (including the legacy-value comparison path). It also preserves the established null-returning contract rather than throwing.\n- The Javadoc on both `toE164` and the new helper was updated to reflect the added rule, consistent with the file's thorough documentation convention.\n\nNo duplication is introduced, no class or method becomes a catch-all, and a maintainer of this codebase would find the placement and idiom natural.",
